# Jekyll includes

- One section per `_includes/` file. `_includes/about.html` only composes them (plus `hr.gradient-line` separators).
- Work and education cards use `.user-details-bis` > `.education-row` > `.education-column`. Logos use `height`/`width="{{ site.icon_size }}"` and a real `alt`.
- Section titles use `.projects-list-title` with an `h1`, matching existing blocks.
- External links: `target="_blank"`. Own products: keep `?ref=adamjaamour` (or the existing `?ref=adamportfolio` on Punto Med).
- Liquid: `{{ site.* }}` and `{% include %}` only. Do not add plugins or collections.
- Large projects / open source: edit the JS data arrays in those includes; do not revive the commented static card markup.
- Privacy modal markup stays in `_includes/footer.html`.
